NAME
       resolved - local caching DNS resolver

SYNOPSIS
       **resolved**

DESCRIPTION
       Listens on UDP 127.0.0.1:53 (domain) and answers DNS queries from local
       programs. /etc/resolv.conf points to it with "nameserver 127.0.0.1".

       Names listed in /etc/hosts are answered directly. Other queries are
       forwarded to the upstream servers and the answers are cached for their
       TTL (at most one hour; failed lookups for one minute). When a server
       does not answer within two seconds, the next one is tried.

       Upstream servers come from /etc/resolved.conf, one "server ADDRESS"
       per line. When it lists none, the DNS servers received from DHCP are
       used. Listing your own servers there bypasses a provider that filters
       DNS.

       Started and restarted by netd(8). Needs root or the NET_BIND
       capability to bind port 53.

FILES
       /etc/resolved.conf, /etc/resolv.conf, /etc/hosts

SEE ALSO
       netd(8), host(1)
